From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: john-zhang1 <john-zhang1@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 0/8] Data Nutrition Label for DSpace 9.2 (backend + Angular UI)

Computes a 0-100 quality score and A-F grade for archived items, stored
as nutrition.* metadata, and shows it as a badge on the item page.

This file holds two patch series for two repositories:

  [PATCH backend 1/4..4/4]  DSpace 9.2 backend (DSpace/DSpace)
  [PATCH angular 1/4..4/4]  DSpace Angular 9.2 UI (DSpace/dspace-angular)

Split it and apply each series to its own repository:

  mkdir dn && git mailsplit -odn data-nutrition.patch
  cd DSpace          && git am --3way $(grep -l '^Subject: \[PATCH backend' ../dn/* | sort)
  cd ../dspace-angular && git am --3way $(grep -l '^Subject: \[PATCH angular' ../dn/* | sort)

(Adjust the ../dn paths to wherever you split the file.)

After applying the backend series, load the schema once and backfill:

  [dspace]/bin/dspace registry-loader -metadata [dspace]/config/registries/nutrition-types.xml
  [dspace]/bin/dspace curate -t datanutrition -i all

If local.cfg overrides event.dispatcher.default.consumers, add
'nutrition' to it. Turn the feature off with nutrition.label.enable = false.

The UI requires the backend series (backend 2/4 exposes
nutrition.label.enable over REST).

-- 
